
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Card payments — BNCTL / Mastercard acquiring
#
# Leave EVERY value below blank and card payment simply does not appear at
# checkout; the existing manual methods (cash, bank transfer, wallet, fiar)
# keep working exactly as before. Nothing here is required to run the store.
#
# >>> Before switching this on, get BNCTL's merchant integration pack and
# >>> confirm the values against it. The adapter in
# >>> src/lib/payments/providers/mpgs.ts is written against the Mastercard
# >>> Payment Gateway Services REST API, which is the usual shape for a bank
# >>> acquiring on the Mastercard network -- but it has NOT been verified
# >>> against BNCTL's own documentation.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Which adapter to use. Only "bnctl" ships today.
# PAYMENT_PROVIDER=bnctl

# Gateway REST host, from BNCTL. No trailing slash.
# MPGS_HOST=https://bnctl.gateway.mastercard.com
# MPGS_MERCHANT_ID=
# MPGS_API_PASSWORD=
# MPGS_API_VERSION=100

# Shared secret used to verify webhook signatures (HMAC-SHA256 over the raw
# body). Without it the webhook endpoint refuses every request -- which is
# the correct default: an unverified webhook that marks orders paid is a
# "mark any order paid" endpoint for anyone who finds the URL.
# MPGS_WEBHOOK_SECRET=
# MPGS_SIGNATURE_HEADER=x-notification-signature

# The gateway's browser-facing origin, added to the Content-Security-Policy
# so the hosted payment page is allowed to load. Usually the same host as
# MPGS_HOST. Without this the payment page is blocked by CSP and the only
# clue is a browser console message your buyer will never read.
# PAYMENT_GATEWAY_ORIGIN=https://bnctl.gateway.mastercard.com

# Shown as the merchant name on the hosted payment page.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_STORE_NAME=Loja AIAI

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Order notifications — an SMS to the buyer's phone, with a one-tap tracking
# link, when their order is placed and each time it moves.
#
# LEAVE EVERYTHING BELOW BLANK AND THE FEATURE STILL WORKS. With no gateway
# configured the store queues every message and shows the admin a one-tap
# "Send SMS" button on the order page (and a queue at /admin/notifications)
# that opens their own phone's SMS app with the number and text already
# filled in. No account anywhere, no signup.
#
# Filling these in makes the same messages send themselves. Nothing else
# changes: same text, same links, same outbox.
#
# >>> SMS is billed per 160-character SEGMENT — and per 70 as soon as the
# >>> message contains a character the GSM-7 alphabet lacks, which in Tetun
# >>> and Portuguese means most accents (ó í ã õ â ê are all absent; é à ì ò
# >>> ù ñ ü ç are present). The admin UI shows the real segment count next to
# >>> every message so this is visible rather than discovered on an invoice.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# --- Option 1: a local Timor-Leste gateway (usually the cheapest for +670) --
#
# Most Timorese operators and regional bulk-SMS resellers offer a plain HTTP
# endpoint. Put the whole request in these variables and no code changes are
# needed. {to}, {to_digits} (no leading +) and {text} are substituted.
#
# Ask your operator — Telemor, Telkomcel or Timor Telecom — for their bulk
# SMS / SMS gateway API. A local route into +670 normally beats an
# international carrier on both price and delivery rate.
#
# NOTE: this URL usually contains the gateway password, so it is a SECRET.
# Keep it in the environment, never in the repository.
# SMS_HTTP_URL=https://gateway.example.tl/send?user=me&pass=secret&to={to_digits}&text={text}
# SMS_HTTP_METHOD=GET
# For POST gateways:
# SMS_HTTP_BODY={"to":"{to}","message":"{text}"}
# SMS_HTTP_CONTENT_TYPE=application/json
# SMS_HTTP_AUTH_HEADER=Bearer abc123
# Many gateways answer HTTP 200 with a body that says "ERROR: no balance".
# Set the string that means success for yours, and anything else counts as a
# failure instead of silently looking sent.
# SMS_HTTP_SUCCESS_TEXT=OK

# --- Option 2: Twilio (global, works immediately, no local contract) --------
#
# Sign up at https://www.twilio.com/console — Account SID and Auth Token are
# both on the dashboard. TWILIO_FROM is either a number you bought, in +E.164,
# or a Messaging Service SID starting with MG.
#
# Trial accounts can only message numbers you have verified in the console,
# which is fine for testing and not for real buyers.
# TWILIO_ACCOUNT_SID=
# TWILIO_AUTH_TOKEN=
# TWILIO_FROM=+15551234567

# Strips the accents GSM-7 does not have (ó -> o) so messages stay at 160
# characters per segment instead of dropping to 70. Off by default, because
# flattening accents is a decision about how the store writes, not a technical
# default worth taking silently. Turning it on roughly halves the cost of
# every message containing one.
# SMS_FORCE_GSM7=true

# Required for the tracking links to be tappable — they go into a text
# message, where a relative path is just text. Without it notifications are
# skipped rather than sent with a broken link.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=https://your-domain.tl

# Already required for admin login; the tracking links are signed with it too,
# so changing it invalidates every link already sitting in buyers' phones.
# SESSION_SECRET=
